#---
# purpose: "decode/1's activation is not yet registered when the recursive component reaching it first walks, so a whole-world membership scan cannot see it; decode/1's ReturnType must never be published by its own AnalyzeActivation walk, only by the solve"
#---
#
# skip_ws/1 is self-recursive. val/1, array/1, and item/1 are a guarded,
# mutually-recursive component (shaped like lib/json.fz's own value parser)
# that each call skip_ws/1 before recursing, and decode_done/2 calls
# skip_ws/1 too, when it forwards to decode_trailing/3. decode/1 hands val/1
# its own input and returns whatever decode_done/2 returns, so decode/1's
# return is itself one more position on skip_ws/1's still-unsettled return --
# a member of that component, not a bystander -- even though decode/1 never
# calls skip_ws/1 directly. decode/1's activation does not exist yet the
# first time the component's own walk runs. A membership answer that scans
# every activation the world currently holds never sees a call site aimed at
# an activation that has not been minted; a local walk starting from the
# component's own facts sees the unresolved call directly and answers
# Unknown until decode/1 exists to be walked, never Alone. Getting this
# wrong makes decode/1 self-publish a ReturnType that a later solve then has
# to clear and republish -- extra work, though every final ReturnType is
# bit-identical either way.
defp skip_ws([:ws | r]), do: skip_ws(r)
defp skip_ws(b), do: b
defp val([:t | r]), do: {:ok, true, r}
defp val([:open | r]), do: array(skip_ws(r))
defp val(b), do: {:error, b}
defp array([:close | r]), do: {:ok, [], r}
defp array(b), do: item(val(b))
defp item({:ok, _v, r}), do: array(skip_ws(r))
defp item(other), do: other
defp decode(input), do: decode_done(val(input), input)
defp decode_done({:ok, v, r}, input), do: decode_trailing(skip_ws(r), v, input)
defp decode_done({:error, b}, input), do: {:error, input, b}
defp decode_trailing([], v, _input), do: {:ok, v}
defp decode_trailing(raw, v, input), do: {:error, input, raw}
def main(), do: dbg(decode([:open, :t, :t, :close]))
